```

⚠️ Do NOT change `components/capture/confirm-form.tsx`. The confirm screen pre-selects the model's draft, so its chips are a correction affordance, not a null-capable input. Divergence between the two is correct here; note it in a brief comment so a future reader does not "fix" the inconsistency.

FINDING 2 — a test name overstates what it checks.

The UI-interaction test in `item-detail.test.tsx` named for carrying all six asserts `fit`, `branding`, `accent_color`, `length` and `distressing` reach `updateItem`, but never selects or asserts `bulk`/Sole. Either extend it to select a Sole value on a Shoes item and assert it reaches the payload, or rename it to say what it actually covers. Extending is better — it is the one path the review could not confirm is non-vacuous.

THEN

Run `npm run test:run` and `npx tsc --noEmit`. No need to re-run `npm run build` or `npm run insights` — neither of these changes touches routing or caching.

